Stand-ins for the four kernel headers src/lfu_filter.h includes when it is
built as part of the lfu_ring module.  They exist so that lfu_filter_eval.c
can be compiled here, in userspace, along the kernel branch of every #if in
that header (-DLFU_KERNEL_TEST) -- which is the only way, short of a lustre
build tree, to notice that the evaluator has picked up a libc dependency it
must not have.  Nothing in here is used by any real build.
